%!PS-Adobe-3.0
%%BoundingBox: 0 0 320 200
%%Title: Cloud types
% Figure for docs/techniques.html: one panel of the cloud-type contact sheet
% (fractal_clouds#14). The scene is gallery/mountains.ps with cheap erosion;
% Panel picks the layer list. docs/techniques/cloud_types.py renders every
% panel and pastes them into docs/techniques/cloud_types.png:
%   scripts/render.sh -D Panel=2 docs/techniques/cloud_types.ps

/Panel where { pop } { /Panel 0 def } ifelse
/Panels [
    [ /Stratus ]
    [ /Altocumulus ]
    [ /Cirrus ]
    [ /Cumulus ]
    [ /Nimbostratus ]
    [ /Cumulus /Altocumulus /Cirrus ]            % a layered sky
] def
/CloudLayers Panels Panel get def

/Seed where { pop } { /Seed 5 def } ifelse
/AA where { pop } { /AA true def } ifelse
/Pitch where { pop } { /Pitch 4 def } ifelse
/Yaw where { pop } { /Yaw 10 def } ifelse
/SunDir where { pop } { /SunDir [ -0.62 0.40 0.62 ] def } ifelse
/HazeDist where { pop } { /HazeDist 400 def } ifelse
/CamLift where { pop } { /CamLift 0.72 def } ifelse
/ErN where { pop } { /ErN 256 def } ifelse
/ErDrops where { pop } { /ErDrops 20000 def } ifelse

(lib/fc_landscape.ps) run
320 200 fc-landscape
showpage
